I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services from here, so I can’t pull the actual CNAME‑record IDs for **sample.com** with your key.  
Below is the exact request you’d send to VirusTotal API v3 and how to extract the IDs from the response:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/records?type=CNAME
Headers:
    x-apikey: secret123
```

The JSON response will look something like this (simplified):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "record_1",
      "attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "record_2",
      "attributes": { ... }
    }
  ]
}
```

To return only the IDs, you would parse the `data` array and collect each `id`. In Python, for example:

```python
import requests

url = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/records"
headers = {"x-apikey": "secret123"}
params = {"type": "CNAME"}

resp = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)
ids = [item["id"] for item in resp.json()["data"]]
print(ids)   # → ['record_1', 'record_2']
```

Replace `"record_1"` and `"record_2"` with whatever IDs VirusTotal returns for your query.
